    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.26187595561460114,
        "y0": 0.6096897741453315,
        "x1": 0.833467702539443,
        "y1": 0.6203796259127203
      },
      "text": "maintaining tonalities, the prevalence of melody and distrust of new languages, codes",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.26187595561460114,
        "y0": 0.622375056209876,
        "x1": 0.8336995114628476,
        "y1": 0.6330649079772648
      },
      "text": "and instruments is common to all regimes of this nature (Leónidas Martín Saura, 2006, p.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.26187595561460114,
        "y0": 0.6353453893889859,
        "x1": 0.2872438334028206,
        "y1": 0.6460352411563747
      },
      "text": "18).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19051938145693964,
        "y0": 0.6634240614420921,
        "x1": 0.8331752244738779,
        "y1": 0.674684038093361
      },
      "text": "2nd Premise: If total sound is imposed in an era in which total essence (revolutionary total",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.6796726636766979,
        "x1": 0.833352810511672,
        "y1": 0.6909326403279669
      },
      "text": "action) is not imposed, this may lead us to totalitarianism. Together with the criticism and rupture",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.6957787041064225,
        "x1": 0.8333497860254975,
        "y1": 0.7070386807576915
      },
      "text": "of lineal, progressive modernity, harmony becomes noise. The acceleration of capitalism brings the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.7120272700934299,
        "x1": 0.8333893093956756,
        "y1": 0.7232872467446989
      },
      "text": "sound of noise (fractured works of art) with it, along with expressiveness which is able to express",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.7282758542042366,
        "x1": 0.5593768597001599,
        "y1": 0.7395358308555056
      },
      "text": "its contradictions. The words we say are also accelerating.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19051938145693964,
        "y0": 0.7444175260232819,
        "x1": 0.731190780970804,
        "y1": 0.7556775026745508
      },
      "text": "Modernity itself brought a contradiction with it, the position of popular culture:",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.7749192322310908,
        "x1": 0.8335685102015118,
        "y1": 0.7856090839984796
      },
      "text": "The Enlightenment believes that the people who must be appealed to in order to legitimise a",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.7876045142956353,
        "x1": 0.833613826231651,
        "y1": 0.7982943660630241
      },
      "text": "secular, democratic government are also the bearers of that which reason wishes to abolish:",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.8004323400412617,
        "x1": 0.8334879255868298,
        "y1": 0.8111221918086505
      },
      "text": "superstition, ignorance and turmoil. Because of this, in Martín Barbero’s words, a complex",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.8132601657868881,
        "x1": 0.8337247582330327,
        "y1": 0.823950017554277
      },
      "text": "system has been developed ‘with abstract inclusion and specific exclusion’. The people are of",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.8260879915325146,
        "x1": 0.8333215275847574,
        "y1": 0.8367778432999033
      },
      "text": "interest in order to legitimise bourgeois hegemony, but are irritating because of their lack of",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23345426951478038,
        "y0": 0.8389158082162413,
        "x1": 0.4840287711762424,
        "y1": 0.8496056599836302
      },
      "text": "culture (García Canclini, 2001, p. 197).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19051938145693964,
        "y0": 0.8669944893312472,
        "x1": 0.8332692398576736,
        "y1": 0.8782544659825161
      },
      "text": "High culture and popular culture. Modernity introduced this dichotomy. High culture is the only",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.8832383159447513,
        "x1": 0.8333971525547381,
        "y1": 0.8944982925960203
      },
      "text": "one which is considered to be culture, the only legitimate culture. Culture was an area for dividing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.8994868909936584,
        "x1": 0.8335513500871576,
        "y1": 0.9107468676449273
      },
      "text": "classes. In Europe, in particular, this mechanism has long been in place (Bourdieu, 1999). In the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.16674057639414908,
        "y0": 0.915592931423383,
        "x1": 0.6694885076538077,
        "y1": 0.9268529080746519
      },
      "text": "world of music, classical music and tonality are the paradigm of art music.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
